{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this","id":1416998,"title":"Changeling Children: How should future supplements deal with this?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-06T08:15:10-07:00","id":1416998,"title":"Changeling Children: How should future supplements deal with this?","content":"There seems to have been recent discussion about what Changeling children might be like. Looking at the Fae-Touched I've been brainstorming some ideas. Most of these are just one quick idea that could be combined with others.<ul><li><u><b>Mein without a Mask:</b></u> Maybe Changeling Children don't have a mask from the Wyrd instead having a more human Mein that is akin to a Stigmatic's Permanent Glitch. For instance a Fire Elemental might have a daughter who has fiery red hair and red eyes.</li> <li><b><u>Strong Sealing:</u></b> Perhaps these children can seal without limitation, even True Fae.</li> <li><b><u>Cold Iron </u></b><b><u>Sensitivity:</u></b> Perhaps these children have the bane of Iron.</li> <li><b><u>Cold Iron </u></b><b><u>Immunity:</u></b> Perhaps these children are unaffected by cold iron.</li> <li><u><b>Contracts with a Price</b></u>: Maybe the Children can use contracts, but instead of having Loopholes they have Catches/Drawbacks.</li> <li><u><b>Glamour</b></u>: Maybe children don't have access to Glamour or perhaps they can only get it from their parents.</li> <li><u><b>Touchstone</b></u>: Maybe these children are always considered a Touchstone and have some sort of special property because of that.</li> <li><b><u>Debt Manipulation:</u></b> Maybe these children can affect how Goblin debt accrues, possibly acting as a buffer for their parent.</li> </ul>My general goal with Changeling children is that they should feel different from Fae-Touch and Changelings. But they should have a sense of being the rock for a Changeling, someone whom the Changeling is attached to at a level that not even the True Fae can destroy.<br /> <br /> What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T01:37:13-07:00","id":1417116,"title":"","content":"Why would Changling Children be mechanically different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T03:49:41-07:00","id":1417122,"title":"","content":"You mean children of the Lost and mortals, not Lost children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T08:43:19-07:00","id":1417148,"title":"","content":"I mean technically at could be the children of Lost and other Lost, or Lost and werewolves, or Lost and... et cetera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T09:14:04-07:00","id":1417155,"title":"","content":"If you have two changelings of different Seemings and Kiths, does the child come out as a combination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T09:23:49-07:00","id":1417156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1417155#post1417155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have two changelings of different Seemings and Kiths, does the child come out as a combination?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the child even come out as a changeling? That's far from guaranteed. For all we know it'd be a mostly human child with some Changeling-esque traits, kinda like Fae-Touched.<br /> The child hasn't gone through any of the processes that turns a human into a changeling so I really don't think the child would become a changeling in turn, nor have a Seeming or Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T15:23:32-07:00","id":1417205,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if two Changelings had a child I'd probably rule that they counted as Fae-touched, with maybe a slight tweak but I'm not sure of that. Assuming, of course, that the changes made to them aren't extensive enough to make procreation nigh impossible, and even then I think two Lost only have a slightly higher chance of conceiving than two kindred.<br /> <br /> Even if it was Changeling+human I don't think I'd make them anything more than a Fae-touched. It already represents 'faerie infkuence without going to Arcadia, why invent the wheel'.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean they have to be standard Fae-touched, by giving them a Merit or two you could have all sorts of fun. Removing the mask of Changelings that they can see? Some human supernatural power merit? The ability to transport entire rooms into the Hedge? You could write up whatever you want and just add the requirement 'at least one parent was a Changeling at conception'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T16:07:05-07:00","id":1417210,"title":"","content":"I don't think Changelings should be able to have children until they fuse with their fetch.<br /> <br /> Connected to this idea, I think it would be interesting for some changelings to have a <i><b>Lost Boys</b></i> template, similar to Summer Time Sam. That is, they don't age and are trapped in the form of a child.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T20:15:24-07:00","id":1417241,"title":"","content":"Drawing on the ideas expressed in Stephen King's <b><i>It</i></b> and the series <b><i>Something is Killing the Children</i></b>, I could easily see Changeling Child or one with the <i>Lost Boy </i> template having the abilities suggested by <i>DontEatRawHagis</i>, because of children's ability to believe in monsters, boogiemen, magic, and Santa Clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T01:49:04-07:00","id":1417286,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for children of Changelings a while back, calling them Wild Child(ren for plural). A Wild Child has two states, Unrealized and Woken. An Unrealized Wild Child is given access to a Seeming blessing and curse, though instead of affecting Clarity it affects Integrity, though they\u2019re not entirely aware of their Seeming Blessing being anything other than coincidences or luck (and as such they can be unreliable). However, unique to fae beings (which they do count as), they cannot innately see past the Mask, even their own. This only changes when they become Woken.<br /> <br /> Attracting the attention of another fae who teaches them ways of the fae, or entering the Hedge enough times, helps them become Woken, at which point their fae mien and Mask properly establishes itself and they can start learning Contracts (their associated Seeming lets them learn appropriate Seeming bonuses like a Changeling). When Woken a Wild Child can see past the Mask, but hazily, and their own mask hides their mien auch that fae can have a hard time noticing them. Wild Children <i>can</i> drop their Mask, but doing so leaves a trail to find them for even longer than a changeling would have.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all I have got for the Wild Children and I doubt that Onyxpath will use those ideas, but hopefully Onyxpath creates something interesting all the same.<br /> <br /> ...I would love for something like this to be in there, but I fear that by posting this it\u2019ll be assured <i>not</i> because of fears of copyright and plagiarism. Le bleh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-08-2020, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T05:12:58-07:00","id":1417307,"title":"","content":"I think the topic of children going through horrifying abuse, maybe people can take this issue with more taste. And the Wyrd doesn\u2019t give a shit about your age. You could try to port the innocent rules from first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T07:58:56-07:00","id":1417321,"title":"","content":"I agree that Changeling children would basically use the rules for Fae-Touched but with Merits representing the Seeming or Kith ancestry. I don't think they should actually have any Seeming, Kith or Mask/Mien. Physically, it's the power of Arcadia, or at the very least the Hedge, that allows human bodies to change. Psychologically, the Durance is a core aspect of a changeling that any child would lack.<br /> That would also keep things simple. Have a generic minor template for Changeling-related humans, but with extra options to customize them.<br /> <br /> I would like also to point out that, despite all the original lore and fluff that WhiteWolf/OnyxPath creates, the core themes of any major and minor splat are always derived from literature, common tropes, myth archetypes etc. The designers usually perform extensive research on the &quot;source material&quot;. I don't have enough culture myself, but I have no doubt that some common staples can be found about Fae children.<br /> So, the answer to the OP's question probably depends on what are the major themes about Fae children in literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T09:52:42-07:00","id":1417335,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26440_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26440\" data-vbnamecard=\"26440\">moonwhisper</a> I am of the opposite mind. These are the direct children of people who have irreversibly been made fae, mind and soul. Whether or not they have a human parent in the mix the child is going to have a <i>much</i> stronger fae inheritance than a Fae Touched is going to ever get without significant outside interference. This is especially in mind when you look at the children of the other splats, who far more often than not have dramatic inheritances as a result. While having merits to represent aspects of them is a fine method, basing them off Fae Touched feels like missing the point of the exercise when they have two completely different sources of empowerment.<br /> <br /> What fae children media would you draw from? Genuinely curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-08-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T06:40:30-07:00","id":1417436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1417307#post1417307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the topic of children going through horrifying abuse, maybe people can take this issue with more taste. And the Wyrd doesn\u2019t give a shit about your age. You could try to port the innocent rules from first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original post makes it pretty clear that this is children born to Changeling parents, specifically the bit about wanting to make them different from both fae-touched and <i>Changelings</i>.<br /> <br /> Changelings made from people who were kidnapped and potentially escaped as children should be normal Changelings, just with an additional host of issues and possibly missing some of those normally possessed by other Changelings,<br /> <br /> Now, of course, a Changeling could always try selling their child to their Keeper in exchange for continued freedom. Possibly one of the biggest potential Clarity breaking points you can think of, but at least your kid will also be a Changeling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:05:44-07:00","id":1417460,"title":"","content":"Wait Lost aren\u2019t sterile in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:18:57-07:00","id":1417465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1417460#post1417460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait Lost aren\u2019t sterile in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lost are fully capable of making babies in 2.0.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:32:26-07:00","id":1417639,"title":"","content":"I would rule it as a normal child with a minor fae &quot;tell&quot;. For instance, the child of an air elemental changeling may occasionally have their wind blow in the wrong direction. But nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T13:37:55-07:00","id":1417898,"title":"","content":"I'm not very experienced with 2E, so most of my input is going to be based off what I recall from 1E, and that would be that such a child is human, though they might get some free merits or access to certain flaws to reflect that parentage. In Mage terms, they *Always* count as Sleepwalkers, and may be Wolf Blooded as well, if the character's characters parentage permits it. Of course, actually becoming a Werewolf, Mage, or Vampire, is something else entirely, and whether such merits are kept afterwards, I would place (very) firmly in the hands of the ST.<br /> <br /> I do recall there being something back in 1E about Ensorcellment, and implementing a merit granting those abilities might not be too far fetched. I haven't read enough about the Fae-Touched in 2E to offer much of an opinion there.<br /> <br /> Edit: Again, not familiar with the current state of 2E, but such characters might have a predisposition towards psychic powers or other forms of Fallen/Hedge Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26456-van-owen","user":"Van Owen","date":". 10-12-2020, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26456-van-owen","name":"Van Owen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T09:53:24-07:00","id":1491486,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the necrobump guys, I find myself revisiting this thread after learning that the children of changelings won't be addressed in kith and kin in any meaningful way. And well, if it doesn't appear in a book that's got 'kin' in the title, three years in, I guess it's fair to expect the CtL2e line will leave this aspect voluntarily unclear for the foreseeable future. <br /> <br /> I must say I'm surprised not to see this discussed more on this forum, as to me it seems a little baffling to make such a humongous change to the original game without any sort of ramifications. <br /> <br /> Am I alone in thinking the ability to have children would be a crucial part of the character's lives and drastically affect changeling society globally? <br /> <br /> If the children of the Lost do have supernatural advantages, wouldn't procreation be encouraged by freeholds by necessity, be it only to even the odds against the Gentry and possible rival domains? <br /> <br /> If there are difficult requirements (such as merging back with the fetch as was suggested in this thread), wouldn't that be an essential right of passage for many members of the courts? <br /> <br /> And if the daughters and sons of changelings end up being wholly mortal, wouldn't that be a tragic dilemma many Lost would have to struggle with? Making the decision to shield them from all things fae or not, staying young as they grow old and die\u2026 <br /> <br /> As much as I adore many of the new ideas that were brought in for 2e, the omission of this core aspect prevents me from getting a clear idea for the setting the developers intended to create. <br /> <br /> So am I alone in this? Is that part of the game just not that important to the rest of you? What house rules have you adopted in your chronicles over the years? <br /> <br /> Oh and while I'm here, big kudos to DontEatRawHagis, some really brilliant ideas in the OP that I will use for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:32:53-07:00","id":1491509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491486#post1491486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the necrobump guys, I find myself revisiting this thread after learning that the children of changelings won't be addressed in kith and kin in any meaningful way. And well, if it doesn't appear in a book that's got 'kin' in the title, three years in, I guess it's fair to expect the CtL2e line will leave this aspect voluntarily unclear for the foreseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kith and Kin was the Player's Guide. It's named for <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kith_and_kin#English\" target=\"_blank\">a phrase</a> that includes a word that Changeling uses as a ludonarrative term, on account of old English words being a major contributor to Lost's lexicon, particularly in 2e (see also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockaigne\" target=\"_blank\">Cockaigne</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummers%27_play\" target=\"_blank\">galoshin</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bethlem_Royal_Hospital\" target=\"_blank\">Bedlam</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hob_(folklore)\" target=\"_blank\">hobgoblin</a>, and so on). I would no more expect the Lost player's guide to talk about changeling fertility from that title than I would expect Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn to talk about forestry from the inclusion of trees in its title.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I alone in thinking the ability to have children would be a crucial part of the character's lives and drastically affect changeling society globally? </div> </div> </div>We really don't need more supernatural eugenics in Changeling after Werewolf and Vampire moved away from specifically entailing it and Demon and Deviant have it as a point of liability or a potential basis for antagonist ideology, and the magical changes to the Lost's physiology being real means being automatically sterile isn't a requirement to lock in the drama of changelings who want kids not being able to have kids. (Even in 1e, childbearing was metaphysically unremarkable enough among the Lost that it was addresses in Rites of Spring's section on Clarity breaking points for extreme unexpected life changes.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the children of the Lost do have supernatural advantages, wouldn't procreation be encouraged by freeholds by necessity, be it only to even the odds against the Gentry and possible rival domains? </div> </div> </div>For much the same reasons 1e talked about when it addressed changelings bearing or siring children, no, trying to meddle in your membership's major life decisions in a way that messes with their self-determination (and thereby their Clarity) is a good way to break your freehold apart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there are difficult requirements (such as merging back with the fetch as was suggested in this thread), wouldn't that be an essential right of passage for many members of the courts?<br /> <br /> And if the daughters and sons of changelings end up being wholly mortal, wouldn't that be a tragic dilemma many Lost would have to struggle with? Making the decision to shield them from all things fae or not, staying young as they grow old and die\u2026<br /> <br /> As much as I adore many of the new ideas that were brought in for 2e, the omission of this core aspect prevents me from getting a clear idea for the setting the developers intended to create. </div> </div> </div>My inference is that the developer's intention, as with <i>many</i> of these sort of things in 2e, is that it's not a consistent enough thing to make definitive statements. Some changelings lack the biomechanical qualities necessary to create progeny. Some changelings are simply sterile. Some are fertile. Some will want to have kids, some will not. Some of the ones who have kids will make babies who are as tied to mundanity as you could hope for in a Touchstone. Some will be touched by the Wyrd and draw worse attention than they'd normally get from associating with a changeling. Some might be the mortal equivalent of a scissor or 1e's fetch-spawn and break down pledges around them.<br /> <br /> Changeling isn't Werewolf, which came into 2e from a previous edition of &quot;werewolves can't have children with each other and the resulting would-be child is a spiritual nemesis that wants to kill them and everyone else&quot;; previous material can still be used with minimal massaging, but Changeling is not a game that particularly relies on the biological children of its supernatural protagonists as a metaphysical talking point.<br /> <br /> The world is wide and strange for the Lost, and covering all those possibilities is beyond the scope of the Player's Guide. You'd want another Night Horrors book for those sorts of things, because Night Horrors is the subline for dealing with weird rare-to-unique phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:25:29-07:00","id":1491527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kith and Kin was the Player's Guide. It's named for <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kith_and_kin#English\" target=\"_blank\">a phrase</a> that includes a word that Changeling uses as a ludonarrative term, on account of old English words being a major contributor to Lost's lexicon, particularly in 2e (see also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cockaigne\" target=\"_blank\">Cockaigne</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummers%27_play\" target=\"_blank\">galoshin</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bethlem_Royal_Hospital\" target=\"_blank\">Bedlam</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hob_(folklore)\" target=\"_blank\">hobgoblin</a>, and so on).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of those things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would no more expect the Lost player's guide to talk about changeling fertility from that title than I would expect Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn to talk about forestry from the inclusion of trees in its title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait doesn't your link actually demonstrate how much the phrase is tied to the concept of family? I feel like I'm missing the point. Regardless I wasn't expecting a clarification on that subject just from the book's title, frankly to me the matter of children was a gaping hole in the setting from the corebook which needed to get patched ASAP.<br /> <br /> Of course I got why it wouldn't be included in oak, but in the player's guide? Is it really that unreasonable to expect a player to ask &quot;hey can my character have kids? Do they get anything unusual?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We really don't need more supernatural eugenics in Changeling after Werewolf and Vampire moved away from specifically entailing it and Demon and Deviant have it as a point of liability or a potential basis for antagonist ideology, and the magical changes to the Lost's physiology being real means being automatically sterile isn't a requirement to lock in the drama of changelings who want kids not being able to have kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable, and a matter of personal preference. Which is why it would be helpful for the devs to weigh in on this one way or another. That being said I'd personally much rather have Changeling focus on what's right for its own setting rather than be influenced by what's been done in other lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Even in 1e, childbearing was metaphysically unremarkable enough among the Lost that it was addresses in Rites of Spring's section on Clarity breaking points for extreme unexpected life changes.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong but the paragraph mentioned the presence of a mortal pregnancy indirectly related to the changeling character, right? Because in that case, yeah it makes sense that it wouldn't be as big as <i>curing the curse infertility of the Lost</i>. Wouldn't that be the stuff of canon-breaking legends in 1e? Nevertheless a Clarity 4 Breaking Point is nothing to sneeze at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For much the same reasons 1e talked about when it addressed changelings bearing or siring children, no, trying to meddle in your membership's major life decisions in a way that messes with their self-determination (and thereby their Clarity) is a good way to break your freehold apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but incentivising does not equate meddling? Although if a particular Court became too intrusive for comfort that could create some mighty fine political tensions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My inference is that the developer's intention, as with <i>many</i> of these sort of things in 2e, is that it's not a consistent enough thing to make definitive statements. Some changelings lack the biomechanical qualities necessary to create progeny. Some changelings are simply sterile. Some are fertile. Some will want to have kids, some will not. Some of the ones who have kids will make babies who are as tied to mundanity as you could hope for in a Touchstone. Some will be touched by the Wyrd and draw worse attention than they'd normally get from associating with a changeling. Some might be the mortal equivalent of a scissor or 1e's fetch-spawn and break down pledges around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I could see it. If that is indeed the dev's intention then just a short paragraph no longer than this one in any sourcebook is all that's required though, isn't it? Leave it open to chaos and the storyteller and players will happily fill in the blanks. Hell just a dev quoting this and saying 'yep that's it' would totally make my day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The reason I'd appreciate something official is I'm always a uneasy at the idea that if I commit to something unconfirmed in a long chronicle, then a new brilliant concept will come along that I'll wish I'd included from the start. And sure you can say that about any new addition to the game, except the ability to have a child is a bit of an unavoidable subject with players, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Well, silver lining is now that Kith is coming out I think can rest easy for a few years on that front.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling isn't Werewolf, which came into 2e from a previous edition of &quot;werewolves can't have children with each other and the resulting would-be child is a spiritual nemesis that wants to kill them and everyone else&quot;;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, Changeling is Changeling and it came into 2e from &quot;you desperately escaped trying to be reunited with your human life, but your infertility will be one of the scars showing how much you've really lost&quot;. And hey perhaps that wasn't Ethan Skemp's original intentions mind you, but that's certainly how my players interpreted it, for good reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">previous material can still be used with minimal massaging, but Changeling is not a game that particularly relies on the biological children of its supernatural protagonists as a metaphysical talking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean obviously, how could it rely on that? 1e had a strict no-exception infertility rule (unless there were alt rules somewhere that I forgot about?) and 2e ignores the subject entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491509#post1491509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world is wide and strange for the Lost, and covering all those possibilities is beyond the scope of the Player's Guide. You'd want another Night Horrors book for those sorts of things, because Night Horrors is the subline for dealing with weird rare-to-unique phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're playing with my feelings, this sounds like one hell of a book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But until then even just a single tiny sentence in Kith would have sufficed, any kind of official &quot;hey it's random, just have fun with it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T18:32:51-07:00","id":1491543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491527#post1491527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait doesn't your link actually demonstrate how much the phrase is tied to the concept of family?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Kith and kin&quot; meaning &quot;friends and family&quot; is pretty definitely sideways to the matter of biological reproduction compared to the more primary point of community and close relationships.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course I got why it wouldn't be included in oak, but in the player's guide? Is it really that unreasonable to expect a player to ask &quot;hey can my character have kids? Do they get anything unusual?&quot; </div> </div> </div>The Demon Player's Guide doesn't spend wordcount talking about the Unchained's demon-blooded children, instead putting the expansion of its corebook's sidebar about the children of demons into a separate supplement detailing the ways those children (including children by adoption via soul pact) interact with Demon's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> The Beast Player's Guide doesn't spend wordcount talking about the Begotten's biological relatives having any supernatural qualities specific to their neck of the metaphysics despite Kinship being a core element of that gameline's approach to monsters; the closest it comes is that one of the ways you can create Horrorspawn is by two beasts controlling their Horrors and having them mate.<br /> <br /> Deviant doesn't spend wordcount talking about the children of deviants, because the transformed are a highly variable phenomenon, &quot;one of your parents/ancestors was one of the Remade&quot; is a provided example of why one might have the Genotypal Origin, and evil lineages and fucked-up eugenicists are both provided examples of antagonists in this game where being able to punch a Nazi is a stated function of the fiction.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e's readdressing of ghoul families in Half-Damned introduces the notion of social ghoul families in addition to the more established biological ghoul families, which are themselves the product of the rare occasions that being a ghoul does not render a person with a uterus unable to bear children and thereby allows the power of stolen life and will invested in them by a vampire to propagate along a line that fits naturally into a metaphysic for which Blood is such a central element. It likewise reexamines dhampir through that same lens as the product of beings who are not alive taking steps to create living children. The game is built in no small part on dynasties and political-familial intrigue as common background radiation when it's not center-stage drama.<br /> <br /> Werewolf 2e, as mentioned, comes from a prior edition where werewolves couldn't have kids with each other and their next-closest confidants had a system in a supplement scaling how likely their kids were to be werewolves. The presence of Pregnancy Conditions in the 2e corebook exists in this context and also the context of 2e allowing any werewolf with 1 Experience and the barest minimum of Honor to acquire functioning reproductive equipment for either set of gametes. Biological family and the expansion thereof are an established part of the game's setting.<br /> <br /> Hunter has the Lucifuge as a major conspiracy based on the penitent descendants of Hell's finest because &quot;children of the devil&quot; is a well-tread fictional trope. Inferno fleshed out what the unrepentant ones can look like slightly later on.<br /> <br /> Promethean addresses the possibility of Prometheans having children with mortals in Magnum Opus, but 1) Magnum Opus was a &quot;secrets and oddities&quot; book for Promethean, 2) Prometheans are rare enough for their personal experiences to be similarly nonstandard even without the chaotic nature of the Divine Fire, and 3) Scions have exactly two mechanical qualities to their condition, one of which is just being to Prometheans as Sleepwalkers are to mages re: being subject to the mental side-effects of their magical powers.<br /> <br /> Mage has Proximi lineages but doesn't provide specific means of producing them without archmagic, Geist doesn't give supernatural progeny any particular focus beyond inborn gifts being one type of prelude to the Bargain in 1e's presentation, and Mummy deals with timespans divorced enough from each other under a tight enough deadline that the question of having kids never really comes up and it doesn't have much source material to base such a concept on in the first place.<br /> <br /> Infrequent mentions of very low fertility rates among the Lost notwithstanding, Changeling is firmly in the same category as these last three \u2014 fictional and loose-mechanical bases for characters to be concerned about the innocence of children does not translate to any outstanding need for special discussion of the reproductive capabilities of post-escape changelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Debatable, and a matter of personal preference. Which is why it would be helpful for the devs to weigh in on this one way or another. That being said I'd personally much rather have Changeling focus on what's right for its own setting rather than be influenced by what's been done in other lines. </div> </div> </div>And it's done that by not inflating something that was barely present in 1e in an edition following on from its contemporaries within the same overall setting also scaling back its focus on the fertility of monsters alongside the franchise's usual avoidance of doing repeat material (there's mechanics of some quantity in roughly half the pre-Demon gamelines concerning supernatural children already).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correct me if I'm wrong but the paragraph mentioned the presence of a mortal pregnancy indirectly related to the changeling character, right? </div> </div> </div>Wrong. &quot;Pregnancy&quot; is the first example given in the parenthetical for that breaking point going back to the corebook, and Rites of Spring's two mentions of pregnancy are in the aforementioned expansion (where it notes that changeling fathers can avoid the breaking point by abandoning their family) and in its sidebar talking about triggering Clarity breaking points from external events (where it mentions that a changeling can't choose to not get pregnant except indirectly by avoiding sexual contact). That's very definitely a statement of &quot;changelings are not universally incapable of having kids.&quot;<br /> <br /> The closest 1e gets is that fetches are usually unable to procreate, as stated in the corebook and reiterated in Autumn Nightmares's section on fetch-children and fetch-spawn (the latter also stating that changelings cannot &quot;normally&quot; have children, which itself reflects the bit in the corebook that &quot;most&quot; changelings aren't able to sire or bear children as a follow-up sentence from the one talking about how changelings' alterations aren't genetic and don't pass on their fae qualities to their children \u2014 and the next sentence makes it clear this is narratively about the Fae continuing to abduct new people instead of maintaining breeding stock, rather than a universal quality of the trauma of becoming fae. The legend of Mother Susan founding the Spring Court is premised on her being infertile and wanting to have a child, but that's an individual character.<br /> <br /> The longest bit of text the line otherwise has on the subject is in a sidebar in Winter Masques, calling back to the bit in the corebook by noting that it's &quot;rare&quot; for changelings to be capable of having kids, then gives the offhand rate of &quot;perhaps one in a hundred&quot; changelings retaining some measure of fertility and says that the resulting kids don't take any influence from their parent's fae features but tend to have odd behavioral quirks and would probably be attractive prizes for the Gentry to carry off.<br /> <br /> Winter Masques was the second supplement in 1e's limited line and, aside from an incidental mention of &quot;those rare few fertile changelings&quot; as the speculative fae ancestors changeling theory/rumor attributes the supernatural abilities of mages, thaumaturges, and psychics to in Rites of Spring's &quot;here's what changelings think are some explanations for non-fae supernatural beings&quot; section, the last time this commonplace infertility showed up in the edition until Goblin Markets, four books past the original planned end of the bookset, where the verbiage is <i>again</i> &quot;most changelings&quot; rather than &quot;all changelings&quot; and the only supernatural qualities that the children gain are drawbacks to the goblin magic used to circumvent a means of overcoming infertility in general, not due to them being born of one of the fae.<br /> <br /> To the extent that this was a major thing, it was clearly not something the line was particularly focused on, and it remains in 2e to the same extend in the same conceptual neighborhood as 1e, where &quot;of course you can't have kids, your organs are made of clockwork&quot; is a natural consequence of the mien diverging from mortal humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, but incentivising does not equate meddling? Although if a particular Court became too intrusive for comfort that could create some mighty fine political tensions. </div> </div> </div>If you are involved enough in someone's life to &quot;incentivize&quot; them to have a child without being closely-associated enough with them to be e.g. living with them, I would find it extremely difficult to classify that as &quot;not meddling.&quot; This is a group of usually twenty to fifty people serving as a support group and/or social safety net for living with the loosely-shared experience of otherworldly trauma that makes them all a little uncomfortable as a society with imprisonment as a punishment or with fixing missing stairs, and a lot of them are going to be leery of any semi-permanent agreement that infringes upon their self-determination, to say nothing of their bodily autonomy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sure you can say that about any new addition to the game, except the ability to have a child is a bit of an unavoidable subject with players, isn't it? </div> </div> </div>I can genuinely say it has literally never come up in any of the games I have played in or run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean obviously, how could it rely on that? 1e had a strict no-exception infertility rule (unless there were alt rules somewhere that I forgot about?) and 2e ignores the subject entirely. </div> </div> </div>See the above breakdown of all the places 1e actually talks about infertility for how not-strict that non-rule was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now you're playing with my feelings, this sounds like one hell of a book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But until then even just a single tiny sentence in Kith would have sufficed, any kind of official &quot;hey it's random, just have fun with it&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I will reiterate that the book does introduce Heirlooms, who are fae-touched who've become so by another one of the Avowed passing down the promise they made to someone who became a changeling, brought up in the section of the book talking about returning to Earth in a different era (or their own pasts).<br /> <br /> It also introduces three alternate Touchstone types in its section on changeling psychology, including Legacy Touchstones (an example of which is &quot;the child [you] raised&quot;), which are harder to detach. The last chapter includes a lengthy section on motleys, and the introduction of the book makes it clear that found family is as valid family as biological relations. &quot;Kin&quot; are well-addressed without needing to discuss what special qualities a changeling's children still don't possess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-28-2022, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T08:45:13-07:00","id":1491602,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Kith and kin&quot; meaning &quot;friends and family&quot; is pretty definitely sideways to the matter of biological reproduction compared to the more primary point of community and close relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don\u2019t understand where you\u2019re going with this, are you trying to say the concept family isn\u2019t related to biological reproduction? Whatever the reason was to avoid the subject of children in the book I think it\u2019s hard to deny it would\u2019ve been a perfect fit thematically. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demon Player's Guide doesn't spend wordcount (...)</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh wow that's thorough ^^ But super interesting to read. I don't really get how do any of these examples make it unthinkable for kith and kin to have a sidebar on procreation however. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Infrequent mentions of very low fertility rates among the Lost notwithstanding, Changeling is firmly in the same category as these last three \u2014 fictional and loose-mechanical bases for characters to be concerned about the innocence of children does not translate to any outstanding need for special discussion of the reproductive capabilities of post-escape changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(...)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And it's done that by not inflating something that was barely present in 1e in an edition following on from its contemporaries within the same overall setting also scaling back its focus on the fertility of monsters alongside the franchise's usual avoidance of doing repeat material (there's mechanics of some quantity in roughly half the pre-Demon gamelines concerning supernatural children already).</span></span>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You seem to be under the impression I\u2019m arguing for a deep dive into the minutiae of changeling reproduction, all I'm really talking about is quick clarification. In a game where characters struggle so much to find balance their human and fae lives, isn\u2019t odd to have absolutely zero info on their ability to have children in 2e? Human things matter a lot to the Lost, and making babies matters a lot to humans. Sure it doesn't have to be a huge part of the setting, but I find it detrimental to leave it as a complete mystery (which as far as I can tell isn\u2019t the case in any of the other lines besides perhaps Mummy). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The longest bit of text the line otherwise has on the subject is in a sidebar in Winter Masques, calling back to the bit in the corebook by noting that it's &quot;rare&quot; for changelings to be capable of having kids, then gives the offhand rate of &quot;perhaps one in a hundred&quot; changelings retaining some measure of fertility and says that the resulting kids don't take any influence from their parent's fae features but tend to have odd behavioral quirks and would probably be attractive prizes for the Gentry to carry off.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oh wow you\u2019re right, 1e was actually much less strict than I remembered on infertility! It\u2019s been so many years. Shows</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> just how perfect that sidebar was though, exactly the kind of thing I\u2019d love to see somewhere, anywhere, for 2e. You see there's no need for a full chapter let alone a full night horror (although these would be nice!), it gives just the right amount of info without taking too much space. And since winter masque was arguably the closest thing 1e ever got to a player\u2019s guide I don\u2019t see why it was so unreasonable to look for something similar in kith and kin. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it remains in 2e to the same extend in the same conceptual neighborhood as 1e, where &quot;of course you can't have kids, your organs are made of clockwork&quot; is a natural consequence of the mien diverging from mortal humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wait are you implying readers are supposed deduce changelings are just as infertile in 2e as in 1e?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are involved enough in someone's life to &quot;incentivize&quot; them to have a child without being closely-associated enough with them to be e.g. living with them, I would find it extremely difficult to classify that as &quot;not meddling.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not really, all you really have to say is \u201cthe choice is yours but we\u2019ll provide\u201d. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can genuinely say it has literally never come up in any of the games I have played in or run.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Really wow that goes to show how differently players can react. Just out of curiosity, did you ever run/play intros to flesh out PCs before they were established in the freehold?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will reiterate that the book does introduce Heirlooms, who are fae-touched who've become so by another one of the Avowed passing down the promise they made to someone who became a changeling, brought up in the section of the book talking about returning to Earth in a different era (or their own pasts).</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Neat idea, but in terms of priorities? That sounds like a one-in-a-million occurrence whereas the ability to procreate affects all changelings. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491543#post1491543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also introduces three alternate Touchstone types are introduces in its section on changeling psychology, including Legacy Touchstones (an example of which is &quot;the child [you] raised), which are harder to detach. The last chapter includes a lengthy section on motleys, and the introduction of the book makes it clear that found family is as valid family as biological relations. &quot;Kin&quot; are well-addressed without needing to discuss what special qualities a changeling's children still don't possess.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Makes it all the more confusing to me why they would dance around the subject and not shed a tiny bit of light on the actual literal \u201ckin\u201d.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T10:14:38-07:00","id":1491620,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491602#post1491602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t understand where you\u2019re going with this, are you trying to say the concept family isn\u2019t related to biological reproduction? Whatever the reason was to avoid the subject of children in the book I think it\u2019s hard to deny it would\u2019ve been a perfect fit thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that biological reproduction is not necessary for a character to have family and a phrase correlating to <i>friends and</i> family is even moreso tangential to the mechanics of birth and conception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh wow that's thorough ^^ But super interesting to read. I don't really get how do any of these examples make it unthinkable for kith and kin to have a sidebar on procreation however. </div> </div> </div>Because procreation is not a major part of Changeling as a gameline, much less to the point of needing addressed in the player's guide specifically.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to be under the impression I\u2019m arguing for a deep dive into the minutiae of changeling reproduction, all I'm really talking about is quick clarification. In a game where characters struggle so much to find balance their human and fae lives, isn\u2019t odd to have absolutely zero info on their ability to have children in 2e? </div> </div> </div>\u2026No? As mentioned, more than half the gamelines barely go into it if they go into it at all, and the ones that <i>do</i> go into it have well-established reasons for doing so.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Human things matter a lot to the Lost, and making babies matters a lot to humans. </div> </div> </div>And a lot of humans are completely uninterested in the process or have reasonable issues with it. The gameline has historically put more emphasis on alienation from one's <i>old</i> family, because changelings were made what they are by being taken from their old lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure it doesn't have to be a huge part of the setting, but I find it detrimental to leave it as a complete mystery (which as far as I can tell isn\u2019t the case in any of the other lines besides perhaps Mummy). </div> </div> </div>Vampires have dhampir and the twisting of life as a thematic element to their game, werewolves are likewise drawing on themes of spiritual and biological family (they have an entire antagonist tribe built on blood lineage as a focal tenet), the main inspiration for Promethean involved its creator destroying the mate he was asked to make for it because he feared the fruits of their union, and demonic bloodlines are a well-tread storytelling trope for the other three lines that care at all about magical heredity. Changeling has consistently given no special consideration for what the children of changelings are like beyond the capacity of those children to be a point of vulnerability and potential desire for them (to the same extent that any group of people with commonplace infertility might want children). It's not a mystery, it's just not remarkable in any sense that isn't an engineered story-hook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh wow you\u2019re right, 1e was actually much less strict than I remembered on infertility! It\u2019s been so many years. Shows just how perfect that sidebar was though, exactly the kind of thing I\u2019d love to see somewhere, anywhere, for 2e. You see there's no need for a full chapter let alone a full night horror (although these would be nice!), it gives just the right amount of info without taking too much space. And since winter masque was arguably the closest thing 1e ever got to a player\u2019s guide I don\u2019t see why it was so unreasonable to look for something similar in kith and kin. </div> </div> </div>Because that sidebar was immediately follow on from a section in that book's chapter about seemings discussing prejudice and the nature of seemings in 1e as the baseline transformations inflicted upon them (and therefore things a character cannot control).</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> Winter Masques was, as it says up front, the book for variety \u2014 its chapters literally break down to examining the three main axes of Changeling character differentiation, including little else besides new kiths, new Courts, and new Contracts for those new Courts and the existing seemings. Rites of Spring falls closer to the niche of &quot;1e player's guide,&quot; given that that's the book exploring tools for player characters to actually use and what various elements of changeling existence feel like in-character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait are you implying readers are supposed deduce changelings are just as infertile in 2e as in 1e? </div> </div> </div>I'm implying that when there's a mini-fiction in the 2e corebook where a character wonders how they would even be able to offer their seventh-born son at the Goblin Market when having genitals hot enough to melt plastic means they aren't sure if they can have a firstborn and no other mention of the fertility of the Lost in particular, people who are not fixated on the topic can draw the reasonable conclusion that it's not important enough to the game to warrant special mention beyond the knock-on effects of the fae mien being real precluding some changelings from having children.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really wow that goes to show how differently players can react. Just out of curiosity, did you ever run/play intros to flesh out PCs before they were established in the freehold? </div> </div> </div>I ran preludes for all four players in my last Changeling game, yes.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neat idea, but in terms of priorities? That sounds like a one-in-a-million occurrence whereas the ability to procreate affects all changelings. </div> </div> </div>My guy, Changeling has had &quot;you came back to Earth much sooner or much later than your subjective experience of time in Arcadia would have indicated&quot; is something with much more folkloric basis and history in the line than &quot;changelings are sterile&quot; and the bigger point of tragedy for the Lost has generally been alienation from the people they used to know, who by definition were born before they emerged from the Thorns. This section in particular is part of the chunk of Chapter 1 talking about unusual routes out of Faerie and through the Hedge, including the Wishing Roads that come out in outer space and the BriarNet connecting to <i>cyberspace</i>. &quot;Fae-touched who inherited their promise&quot; was a thing the 2e corebook mentioned and that is a relevant curiosity to elaborate upon when the prospect of coming out generations or centuries after your abduction is on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Makes it all the more confusing to me why they would dance around the subject and not shed a tiny bit of light on the actual literal \u201ckin\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Because it's not a mystery and there's no existing section in the book where such a clarification would actually be suitably-placed.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T13:50:33-07:00","id":1491644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying that biological reproduction is not necessary for a character to have family and a phrase correlating to <i>friends and</i> family is even moreso tangential to the mechanics of birth and conception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, well on the one hand I agree the title wasn't false advertising or anything, but on the other hand the way you're trying to frame it as &quot;preposterous! family has nothing to do with your own children!&quot; seems a bit convoluted to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because procreation is not a major part of Changeling as a gameline, much less to the point of needing addressed in the player's guide specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not advocating for procreation to be a major part of Changeling, that's a strawman. I do think it needs to be at least briefly addressed <i>somewhere</i>, because it's a crucial aspect missing from the corebook, and so the player's guide is a bit of a missed opportunity in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026No? As mentioned, more than half the gamelines barely go into it if they go into it at all, and the ones that <i>do</i> go into it have well-established reasons for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be happy if 2e barely got into it instead of not at all. If anything I'm jealous of most of the things you've listed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a lot of humans are completely uninterested in the process or have reasonable issues with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and? The point still stands that it's a major aspect of human society, and the decision to have a child or not would be a heavy one to proportionally as many changelings, if not more depending on specifics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The gameline has historically put more emphasis on alienation from one's <i>old</i> family, because changelings were made what they are by being taken from their old lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why not keep them at a 99% infertility rate and call it a day? Why make the change at all if the children of changelings are to be completely disregarded as utterly unimportant?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that sidebar was immediately follow on from a section in that book's chapter about seemings discussing prejudice and the nature of seemings in 1e as the baseline transformations inflicted upon them (and therefore things a character cannot control).</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly many of the things related to the 'kin' theme you mentioned seem just as loosely related as that section of masques, so to me at least it'd feel perfectly at home there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Winter Masques was, as it says up front, the book for variety \u2014 its chapters literally break down to examining the three main axes of Changeling character differentiation, including little else besides new kiths, new Courts, and new Contracts for those new Courts and the existing seemings. Rites of Spring falls closer to the niche of &quot;1e player's guide,&quot; given that that's the book exploring tools for player characters to actually use and what various elements of changeling existence feel like in-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly debatable, while rites of spring had many useful things for players, a lot of it was obviously intended for STs. Winter masques was all about giving players more options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm implying that when there's a mini-fiction in the 2e corebook where a character wonders how they would even be able to offer their seventh-born son at the Goblin Market when having genitals hot enough to melt plastic means they aren't sure if they can have a firstborn and no other mention of the fertility of the Lost in particular, people who are not fixated on the topic can draw the reasonable conclusion that it's not important enough to the game to warrant special mention beyond the knock-on effects of the fae mien being real precluding some changelings from having children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, imagine if you will a ST starting fresh on 2e, trying to determine if one of his PCs can make an NPC pregnant or not. Not an especially far-fetched situation, right? What you're saying is it's perfectly normal for them to have to get an answer based on the uncertainties of some random character buried in a mini-fiction. Come on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guy, Changeling has had &quot;you came back to Earth much sooner or much later than your subjective experience of time in Arcadia would have indicated&quot; is something with much more folkloric basis and history in the line than &quot;changelings are sterile&quot; and the bigger point of tragedy for the Lost has generally been alienation from the people they used to know, who by definition were born before they emerged from the Thorns. This section in particular is part of the chunk of Chapter 1 talking about unusual routes out of Faerie and through the Hedge, including the Wishing Roads that come out in outer space and the BriarNet connecting to <i>cyberspace</i>. &quot;Fae-touched who inherited their promise&quot; was a thing the 2e corebook mentioned and that is a relevant curiosity to elaborate upon when the prospect of coming out generations or centuries after your abduction is on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure I love the idea and how it fits in the themes of the line, but how many times would you realistically encounter such a rare fae-touched compared to children of changelings, now that they're allegedly mostly fertile?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491620#post1491620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Because it's not a mystery and there's no existing section in the book where such a clarification would actually be suitably-placed.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>If no one can answer with certainty how it's supposed to work in 2e, then yes it is a mystery. And to my dismay it seems like it will probably remain one for years to come.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T15:32:42-07:00","id":1491666,"title":"","content":"You're making a mountain out of a molehill here.<br /> <br /> 2e Lost deal with pregnancy as dramatically and group appropriate. Since it's not important to the world building of the game, it receives no special attention. The CofD 2e core book for mortals don't give you any big discussion on pregnancy, and that's amount making humans. Beast, another game where family is a huge deal, again doesn't really bother with anything specific about pregnancy and child birth.<br /> <br /> If you want pregnancy to matter in your Lost games, all the tools you need are there. If you don't, all the tools are there. Since the question doesn't have an important thematic answer, the game leaves it to the group to decide what happens in their game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T19:18:50-07:00","id":1491700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491644#post1491644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure I love the idea and how it fits in the themes of the line, but how many times would you realistically encounter such a rare fae-touched compared to children of changelings, now that they're allegedly mostly fertile?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to talk about strawmen, it would really behoove you to not turn &quot;the closest thing Changeling 2e has to a concrete statement on the fertility of its titular characters in the vein of the very small information 1e had on it is an example of one of them probably not being able to have kids because the necessary bodily equipment for them to do so is hot enough to melt plastic&quot; into an &quot;allegation&quot; that changelings are now &quot;mostly fertile.&quot; No longer being mostly infertile does not imply the opposite is now necessarily true.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't make a statement about how many changelings are fertile. It states that the transformations wrought upon the Lost by their durance and their lives thereafter are real, when those transformations include partaking of the nature of a whole bunch of things that can't produce human children. Those transformations exist within the medium of a highly context-sensitive occult system explicitly designated as too complex for any one person to fully comprehend. Sometimes those transformations and/or that magic will still allow a changeling to bear or sire children, sometimes they will not, and the determining factors for that are entirely within the players' hands as things they are or are not interested in dealing with.<br /> <br /> The line's folkloric truck with childbearing most significantly involves generational agreements, specifications of birth order (for exchange or as a qualification for a task), and people who are unable to conceive children going to desperate measures to have children. Most of this involves supernatural agreements and/or agreements with supernatural beings, and fae-touched are the place that tends to live.<br /> <br /> A fae-touched is a person who has kept an important promise to someone who became a changeling, ventured into the Hedge to try and find them, and managed to get out again with an abiding connection to the Wyrd; it's already possible that the person in question is actually a relative of the one who actually kept the promise, and an Heirloom is someone who swore a blood oath with one of the Avowed in the Hedge to find the changeling and uphold the promise. Even without particularly far-reaching escape timelines, changelings have longer lifespans than mortals do; Heirloom creation is regarded by some of the Avowed as tantamount to giving up on their changeling to the point that some only do so on their deathbeds, which lends itself to another commonly familial trope that doesn't require biological relation: the last will and testament, here also feeding into the recurring pattern in fae things in particular for the price of freeing one individual from bondage to require putting another in their place (see also Goblin Queens having an exit clause of &quot;pass the mantle on to a mortal child&quot;).<br /> <br /> There are no consistent game-mechanical effects to changelings being fertile or infertile or being the child of one of them and there never have been even in the edition of the game where it was discussed to any degree (which, again, amounts to three partial lines in three different books and a sidebar saying they're rare but not particularly special beyond that rarity).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, imagine if you will a ST starting fresh on 2e, trying to determine if one of his PCs can make an NPC pregnant or not. Not an especially far-fetched situation, right? What you're saying is it's perfectly normal for them to have to get an answer based on the uncertainties of some random character buried in a mini-fiction. Come on. </div> </div> </div>It is frankly an extremely weird thing to be this fixated on given how little attention the line ever gave it, because <i>yes, this is an especially far-fetched situation</i>. Most RPG players I know don't talk a whole lot about their characters' ability to have children without the presence of a game element relating to it. Changelings aren't the Dragon-Blooded Exalted, nor is Lost a Crusader Kings-style dynasty simulator. As HeavyArms notes above, bluebook Chronicles of Darkness games don't deal with childbirth as an assumed common element either. Neither I nor most of my players are particularly interested in pursuing romantic plot threads with PCs, much less sexual consummation and the consequences thereof, and I don't think we're particularly uncommon in that regard.<br /> <br /> 2e has notably shifted Clarity away from being imperiled by life changes as a general phenomenon to being endangered by the loss of Touchstones and people undermining your confidence in the truth of your experiences, so surprise pregnancies aren't going to be an assumed source of Clarity damage anyway; meanwhile, if a player wants their character to be trying to start a biological family, it's as down to agreement between them and the ST as it would be in 1e if difficulties in conceiving were a narrative device they were interested in or not.<br /> <br /> This is a niche issue. You use your own discretion like you would for any other niche issue. It is perfectly normal to come to a decision based on your preferences and the needs of your group without needing a specific ruling from the text. <i>Come on.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T06:06:09-07:00","id":1491750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is frankly an extremely weird thing to be this fixated on given how little attention the line ever gave it, because <i>yes, this is an especially far-fetched situation</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was weird when 1e spent any amount of time on the fetch-babies situation, but I figured that because children of faeries features not inconsequentially in folklore that the folk at Onyx Path of that era wanted to introduce the concept somewhere in here.<br /> <br /> I would leave it entirely to the table to decide what it means and what to do with it, but the &quot;make them kind of fae-touched&quot; is my favorite suggestion so far.<br /> <br /> Also: Far-&quot;Fetched&quot;. Heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T09:20:36-07:00","id":1491770,"title":"","content":"Good news everyone! Looks like we actually had some sort of official stance on the issue all along, you may remember <a href=\"https://thestorytold.libsyn.com/episode-29-meghan-fitzgerald-interview\" target=\"_blank\">this here interview</a> from a few years back. In it, Meghan Fitzgerald does confirm that she and Rose Bailey made the deliberate decision to let changelings (and fetches) freely have babies in 2e, and that the intention was to make them \u201cspecial\u201d, in a way she hoped to develop in future books. Now whether you agree with that approach or not, at least we\u2019re past twisting the text like a bretzel to try and make sense of what the devs were aiming for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're making a mountain out of a molehill here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty as charged ( \u0361\u00b0 \u1d25 \u0361\u00b0)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e Lost deal with pregnancy as dramatically and group appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently yes, pending some new mechanics that may or may not be published down the line. However by omitting the subject entirely to keep things open, the unfortunate side effect is the game never communicates that you\u2019re supposed to work this aspect out with your group, for now. I think it\u2019s a bit clumsy and that it must be confusing for at least some STs trying to get into the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's not important to the world building of the game, it receives no special attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, sure, the odds of the 1% fertile changelings actually finding out they can have a child, and wanting to have one, and then finding the right circumstances to do so, are astronomical.<br /> <br /> Now in 2e, I agree that as things stand it\u2019s probably the easiest path not to think too much about how changeling fertility would affect the worldbuilding, and on the rare occasion where a PC would want a child just play it by ear. That seems to work perfectly for everyone, so god bless.<br /> <br /> That being said if you take a moment so think about fertility as the norm and drive that to its logical conclusion, then I think it changes the setting more than you would expect, especially if the children are &quot;special&quot;. We\u2019re potentially talking about adding several generations of \u201cfae-touched\u201d children (for lack of a better term) to every freehold! That\u2019s a humongous change in the societies of the few and vulnerable changelings who made it back to earth. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The CofD 2e core book for mortals don't give you any big discussion on pregnancy, and that's amount making humans. Beast, another game where family is a huge deal, again doesn't really bother with anything specific about pregnancy and child birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Procreation affects human society to its core as well, we just happen to have reality as a sourcebook for that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast, another game where family is a huge deal, again doesn't really bother with anything specific about pregnancy and child birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well maybe I should go to the Beast forum to complain about that. Just kidding. Or am I?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491666#post1491666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want pregnancy to matter in your Lost games, all the tools you need are there. If you don't, all the tools are there. Since the question doesn't have an important thematic answer, the game leaves it to the group to decide what happens in their game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wellll... Actually the game doesn\u2019t provide any tools for that, quite the opposite, it just leaves it blank. Unless you meant a blank page and our collective imaginations are the only tools we\u2019ll ever need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to talk about strawmen, it would really behoove you to not turn &quot;the closest thing Changeling 2e has to a concrete statement on the fertility of its titular characters in the vein of the very small information 1e had on it is an example of one of them probably not being able to have kids because the necessary bodily equipment for them to do so is hot enough to melt plastic&quot; into an &quot;allegation&quot; that changelings are now &quot;mostly fertile.&quot; No longer being mostly infertile does not imply the opposite is now necessarily true.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't make a statement about how many changelings are fertile. It states that the transformations wrought upon the Lost by their durance and their lives thereafter are real, when those transformations include partaking of the nature of a whole bunch of things that can't produce human children. Those transformations exist within the medium of a highly context-sensitive occult system explicitly designated as too complex for any one person to fully comprehend. Sometimes those transformations and/or that magic will still allow a changeling to bear or sire children, sometimes they will not, and the determining factors for that are entirely within the players' hands as things they are or are not interested in dealing with.<br /> <br /> The line's folkloric truck with childbearing most significantly involves generational agreements, specifications of birth order (for exchange or as a qualification for a task), and people who are unable to conceive children going to desperate measures to have children. Most of this involves supernatural agreements and/or agreements with supernatural beings, and fae-touched are the place that tends to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, judging by the aforementioned interview you seem to have misread the scriptures a bit on that one. But to be fair I really like your idea of basing fertility on what reproductive organs remain intact, and at least it\u2019s based on something that exists in 2e, even though fictions take too much creative license (as they should!) to be a reliable source in RPG books. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fae-touched is a person who has kept an important promise to someone who became a changeling, ventured into the Hedge to try and find them, and managed to get out again with an abiding connection to the Wyrd; it's already possible that the person in question is actually a relative of the one who actually kept the promise, and an Heirloom is someone who swore a blood oath with one of the Avowed in the Hedge to find the changeling and uphold the promise. Even without particularly far-reaching escape timelines, changelings have longer lifespans than mortals do; Heirloom creation is regarded by some of the Avowed as tantamount to giving up on their changeling to the point that some only do so on their deathbeds, which lends itself to another commonly familial trope that doesn't require biological relation: the last will and testament, here also feeding into the recurring pattern in fae things in particular for the price of freeing one individual from bondage to require putting another in their place (see also Goblin Queens having an exit clause of &quot;pass the mantle on to a mortal child&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Heirloom is a beautiful concept for a once-in-a-chronicle NPC. Maybe two, but that\u2019s pushing it. I like it a lot though!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no consistent game-mechanical effects to changelings being fertile or infertile or being the child of one of them and there never have been even in the edition of the game where it was discussed to any degree (which, again, amounts to three partial lines in three different books and a sidebar saying they're rare but not particularly special beyond that rarity).</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ve described my issue with 2e in a nutshell. As for 1e I thought it was perfect on handling the matter of progeny, doing exactly what it was trying to do in a very clear way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is frankly an extremely weird thing to be this fixated on given how little attention the line ever gave it, because <i>yes, this is an especially far-fetched situation</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491700#post1491700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither I nor most of my players are particularly interested in pursuing romantic plot threads with PCs, much less sexual consummation and the consequences thereof, and I don't think we're particularly uncommon in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>More power to you guys. Your particular PCs are one thing, but as STs we\u2019re expected to portray a realistic world where not every NPC is an asexual monk, and hate it all you want but humans are supremely sexual beings. Now add the spring court to the mix and tell me with a straight face sexuality is unheard of in CtL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T09:33:19-07:00","id":1491775,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that Changelings are now able to have children in the revised edition and adds a new layer to player character drama. I remember that they just lightly touched on it in the 1st edition and commented that such children would be a big event for the Freehold and for the most part would differ little from other kids though they might have odd quirks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:29:41-07:00","id":1491809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491770#post1491770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news everyone! Looks like we actually had some sort of official stance on the issue all along, you may remember <a href=\"https://thestorytold.libsyn.com/episode-29-meghan-fitzgerald-interview\" target=\"_blank\">this here interview</a> from a few years back. In it, Meghan Fitzgerald does confirm that she and Rose Bailey made the deliberate decision to let changelings (and fetches) freely have babies in 2e, and that the intention was to make them \u201cspecial\u201d, in a way she hoped to develop in future books. Now whether you agree with that approach or not, at least we\u2019re past twisting the text like a bretzel to try and make sense of what the devs were aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I was going ignore this thread, but this little bit here bothers me, so I feel it should be laid out:<br /> <br /> That Meghan and Rose have mentioned that this is a subject they want to develop further in future books <i>has no bearing</i> on the fact that you're raising a fuss over it not being a subject of interest in the books released since the Changeling 2E core release, and it has <i>no bearing </i>on what's going to be more the priority for the two books that have released since then. Kith &amp; Kin, in particular, has been a book that's been in development since <i>even before the current Changeling 2E Core was finished, </i>and it's prioritzation was always geared towards what was going to be more important for players. That, in all that time, we ended up with a product that doesn't have details on pregnancy and special changeling babies <i>should answer the question to begin with</i>. It's also rude to imply that since Meghan and Rose said it, they can't then change their mind, or otherwise have to be held for it even in scenarios in the future where it's not really a viable course of action, such as Paradox simply saying no. I dislike the overblowing of this &quot;find&quot;, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> Also, since we're here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More power to you guys. Your particular PCs are one thing, but as STs we\u2019re expected to portray a realistic world where not every NPC is an asexual monk, and hate it all you want but humans are supremely sexual beings. Now add the spring court to the mix and tell me with a straight face sexuality is unheard of in CtL. </div> </div> </div>Speaking as one of those players and one of the people who strongly and personally suggested that the BPG should have Horrorspawn in it, I have to say that your understanding of the issue is really sorely lacking. I personally enjoy games that do have romance, sex and sexuality(One of my favorite characters, who contributed towards my transition, had sex as one of their preferred stress relievers, and had a character arc that involved her reconciling her bisexuality and homoromanticism with her previously ironclad understanding of self), and even pregnancy, and this is something shared by the players in our group-but not all games need that, not all groups are comfortable with that. For Satchel's group in particular, it didn't fit into our characters when we started-two of our characters are children, and the other two have got their own problems that would be distracted from if we also worried about their love life. It just doesn't fit our themes and interests for this game.<br /> <br /> Spring Court may has sexuality as a part of it's core of desire, but to bring that up as though that's the whole of the point is it's own form of immaturity. Positing that games need to include or feature sex to be realized is immature in the same-and-equal vein of thinking that all games must be sexless.<br /> <br /> Chronicles has grown up with it's audience, and I think it's really cool that they have, across various products, been willing to discuss and work in themes and stories of parenthood into it-but most gamelines that aren't about that to begin with usually aren't going to have it be a hot topic must-play thing. It's a cool thing to have, but it's not a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> It's also not a hard thing to homebrew in the meantime. Honestly, I get more out of the parent-child relationship if they child is just <i>human, </i>both positive and negative-but between the Fae Touched Template, easy application of 1e and 2e material, and now Heirlooms, I can just make implement Wyrd babies if I run a game that needs it.<br /> <br /> I also have to ask how this material is important to any game you are running or about to run, because if this is just general interest, the sheer personal thrashing on the subject seems excessive, and given the initial post seemed excited by eugenically-interested freeholds and how this interest in children has slowly translated into a more sex-oriented concern, I'm not gonna lie, it's also started at creepy and is steadily getting worse. I trust that's not the impression you want to actually give, so some context in how this <i>actually matters</i> to your table might help.<br /> <br /> But yeah, otherwise, like, yes, I too am excited to see if and how Changeling handles the topic-hell, I would enjoy writing it. Do I need it now? No, not really. Do I think most players need it? No, not really. I, and I imagine the majority of the player base, will be pleasantly surprised when(/if) it comes up, and but in the meantime, we're not exactly stopped by it's lack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-29-2022, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T13:53:31-07:00","id":1491813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491770#post1491770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guilty as charged</div> </div> </div> </div>Then perhaps it might work better to tone it back a bit? It should be abundantly clear that you're not going to get Satchel or I to sudden see your view point as superior with this approach. I don't think being so hyperbolic is doing any service to people that share your essential concerns/issues either, because it's distracting from any sort of nuanced conversation about how to handle children in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However by omitting the subject entirely to keep things open, the unfortunate side effect is the game never communicates that you\u2019re supposed to work this aspect out with your group, for now. </div> </div> </div>This is something that's become standard for my groups to work out for decades now. It's entirely because of games that make (frequently needlessly) child bearing a big deal in the game, that it's become a standard subject for me to seek group consensus on how to handle because players felt pressured into getting into areas they didn't enjoy via games like Werewolf or Exalted (not even getting into horror stories of GMs forcing kids on PCs) and the base setting making kids a big picture focus of the games on some level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That being said if you take a moment so think about fertility as the norm and drive that to its logical conclusion, then I think it changes the setting more than you would expect, especially if the children are &quot;special&quot;. We\u2019re potentially talking about adding several generations of \u201cfae-touched\u201d children (for lack of a better term) to every freehold! That\u2019s a humongous change in the societies of the few and vulnerable changelings who made it back to earth. </div> </div> </div>Not particularly.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, Uratha society didn't actually radically change despite 2e allowing Uratha to have kids with other Uratha, and vastly expanding the concept of &quot;pack&quot; to include Wolf-Blooded and humans by default (with the potential to start including non-human animals and other supernaturals). That's because Forsaken 1e already presumed that Uratha had a support group of Wolf-Blooded that were part of a large community of human. The shift just made that integration more comprehensive.<br /> <br /> 1e changelings did not live in isolated Freeholds that were completely separate from humanity (that would have just destroyed them all with Clarity loss and Glamour shortages). Changelins were always supposed to be part of Freeholds deeply invested in their local communities. The Lost make new found families to replace their old families and friends, centered around the Freehold yes, but not limited to it. A motley that runs an adoption agency (an example from one of my 1e games) to get out their desire for being part of creating full families meant generations of kids with direct connections to the Freehold (and not purely for good, as that was a weakness the Gentry have not moral compunctions about abusing). 2e making fertile changelings less rare might shift some of the dynamics around, but in the end that only serves the overarching purpose of Freeholds as integrated parts of a community that help ground the Lost in the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Procreation affects human society to its core as well, we just happen to have reality as a sourcebook for that. </div> </div> </div>In the reality sourcebook, please point me to where we're told how to adjudicate the frequency of humans born with Supernatural Merits from the CofD 2e core book.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps, going back to your admitting guilt to overdoing this, let it go and move on from this idea that a lack of specifics is a real problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well maybe I should go to the Beast forum to complain about that. Just kidding. Or am I? </div> </div> </div>Unless you feel like adding to the number of posters that are willing to thoroughly dissect and reject your posts, I hope you are kidding. The Beast forum has seen a lot of threads that have finely honed Beast fans' knives when in comes to people that decide to just saunter in and start complaining with half-assed nonsense.<br /> <br /> Also, do remember that joking in text is difficult as humor does not communicate easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wellll... Actually the game doesn\u2019t provide any tools for that, quite the opposite, it just leaves it blank. Unless you meant a blank page and our collective imaginations are the only tools we\u2019ll ever need. </div> </div> </div>Aspirations, Conditions, a basic resolution mechanic, Lost specific subsystems that can be brought in as desired, and so on is, in fact, not blank, and more than sufficient tools for dealing with pregnancy, birth, and child rearing in game.<br /> <br /> Have you run a CofD 2e game where any of the PCs have had a child? I have. It wasn't hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You\u2019ve described my issue with 2e in a nutshell. As for 1e I thought it was perfect on handling the matter of progeny, doing exactly what it was trying to do in a very clear way. </div> </div> </div>This is internally contradictory as a statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More power to you guys. Your particular PCs are one thing, but as STs we\u2019re expected to portray a realistic world where not every NPC is an asexual monk, and hate it all you want but humans are supremely sexual beings. Now add the spring court to the mix and tell me with a straight face sexuality is unheard of in CtL. </div> </div> </div>Satchel didn't say sexuality. Satchel said that it's rare to actually play out romance and the results of romance &quot;on screen&quot; in TT RPG games where you have a GM/etc. and 3-6 other people sitting around a table/on video chat/whatever.<br /> <br /> Having characters with overtly discussed sexuality, strong libidos, hopeless romantic dreams, and so on are very common. Actively playing it out in front of the rest of your group is not. Even in games I've been in where romantic play was a normal activity, it was something reserved for time apart from main play.<br /> <br /> I assure you this has nothing to do with hating human sexual proclivity, or failing to appreciate the responsibilities of the ST. If anything it's the duty of the ST at work: the ST's job is to make the game about the PCs, not spend 30 minutes describing the Spring Monarch's latest display of sexual prowess, or spend a hour of play time having a Winter courtier discuss all the fine details involved in seeing to the needs of child rearing to a Lost that missed out on that education thanks to their Keeper. Most people would see it as the ST's job to provide that those details exist, but move past them quickly to focus on what matters to the PCs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T14:28:03-07:00","id":1491816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1416998-changeling-children-how-should-future-supplements-deal-with-this?p=1491770#post1491770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More power to you guys. Your particular PCs are one thing, but as STs we\u2019re expected to portray a realistic world where not every NPC is an asexual monk, and hate it all you want but humans are supremely sexual beings. Now add the spring court to the mix and tell me with a straight face sexuality is unheard of in CtL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even as a monkish asexual, I can firmly say that going into detail about your characters sexual exploits is magical realm territory, but otherwise no-one cares if you want to have your character do the dirty off-screen. Which is all the more reason for the question of conception to be ST fiat, since unexpected children CAN be an interesting story hook, if handled respectfully. Not every ST is going to be comfortable doing so, and it will likely have been a boundry discussed at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T14:49:57-07:00","id":1491820,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Thread necromancy.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}